a recent wb job posting appears to  indicate hogwarts legacy  could be a live service game and the  internet  is freaking out i'll get you caught up  on the news why i  actually think it could be a good thing  and what even is  a live service game all that and more in  today's hogwarts legacy video  people of the internet retroaction tour  here if we're meeting for the first time  i'm just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and a few like me are looking  forward to hogwarts legacy  then be sure and give this video a like  before you go it helps me know you guys  are enjoying the hogwarts legacy content  and want to see  even more of it today's video is broken  down into four different sections we'll  start by talking about wb's focus  on live service games and why hogwarts  legacy could be a part of that push  how we should define live service games  what the concerns would be for hogwarts  legacy  and then finally i'll give you a few  ideas i have for how hogwarts legacy can  be an absolutely phenomenal live service  title  i'll include timestamps for each of  these different sections and you can  also use the chapter markers in the  timeline if you're just interested in a  specific section of the video  to start off why are we even talking  about hogwarts legacy as a live service  game  well back in late january there was a  job posting on wb's career site for a  virtual  games production mba intern for the  summer of 2021  and at the time of recording this video  the ad actually is still available  online so if you do want to read it for  yourself you can do that at this time  i'll post a link down in the description  of course i'll also include screenshots  here in the video to any important  sections that we need to discuss  to be honest with you guys there's a lot  here in this job posting for us to break  down  here's the first bit that stands out to  me the wbie which stands for warner  brothers interactive entertainment  production summer intern will have the  opportunity to learn about the way a  game publisher  evaluates new game opportunities  remember that by working closely with  the executive producer  wbie is currently involved in a variety  of new projects ranging from casual  games to core games featuring our  well-known franchises on all platforms  console digital mobile with a heavy  focus  on live service so there you go  that is what tipped a lot of folks off  and has everyone asking  hey does this apply to hogwarts legacy  and if so what does that mean  for the story this was supposed to be a  single player story game  what's going on here now if you just  looked at that alone you might think  well hey hogwarts legacy is delayed  until 2022  it's probably not included in this  considering this position is for an  internship during the summer of 2021  well let's keep reading from the listing  so we can see a little more about what  this intern will be doing  so some of the tasks for the inter will  include drive competitive research  tear downs genre analysis and benchmarks  of  external games and market trends to  support project green lights and  translate best practices into  actionable product strategies and then  it goes on to say participate in initial  developer diligence meetings  assistance and setting up demos on a  variety of different hardware  playthroughs of various game demos  write-ups on game demos both from a  gameplay  and market opportunity perspective so it  seems  pretty clear to me that this job is  going to be heavily focused on  gathering information and conducting  research on what maybe  other companies are doing and even  helping setting up demos  so to me all of this speaks to planning  something that is not  ready for release right now but how can  we maybe add live service elements  to what we've got so what other games  could wb possibly be talking about here  we know they mentioned quote well-known  franchises and if you look at the titles  they're releasing this year i would say  two of them fall into that category  there's lego star wars the skywalker  saga back for blood and gotham knights  now back for blood looks promising but  it would be a stretch to call it a  well-known franchise since it's brand  new both star wars and gotham knights  though  absolutely they certainly fit the bill  that being said when it comes to live  service the lego star wars games are  well known quantities at this point they  have a tried and true formula that works  so it would be pretty strange to me if  we saw them add some sort of live  service component  there with a lego game it's possible but  it would just surprise me  of those three that i just mentioned i  think gotham knights is clearly the most  likely title to receive strong support  after launch with live service elements  but would this job posting really only  focus  on one live service title the listing  clearly indicates more than just  one so in that case i think we have to  look at hogwarts legacy as well as the  2022 suicide squad game as other  potential candidates  now it's entirely possible hogwarts  legacy isn't part of the live service  push at all but with it already getting  a lengthy delay to 2022 and wb seemingly  placing a focus on live service  i think it's safe to say that it will  indeed happen  and i actually think it could be a good  thing of course i always want to hear  from you guys and today i'd love to know  if there are any games you play  regularly that you would consider to be  a live service game let me know down in  the comments  i also think it's helpful if we can try  to define what wb considers to be a  live service game this isn't a brand new  term but i do feel like it's one we're  seeing more of  lately and there's still a lot of  confusion as to what people actually  mean when they're saying  live service i will say that for me  personally whenever i think of live  service i think of something like  destiny world of warcraft or even  fortnite these are titles that  consistently release new content  and regular updates to their game it  just so happens that all three are also  heavily focused on multiplayer with  various cooperative and competitive  elements  in fact in my mind i've always thought  of live service games as being titles  that focus primarily on multiplayer  but that doesn't always have to be the  case there actually is a wikipedia entry  for  games as a service and here's how they  define it there  in the video game industry games as a  service represents providing video games  or game content on a continuing  revenue model similar to software as a  service  games as a service are ways to monetize  video games either after their initial  sale  or to support a free to play model games  released under the games as a service  model typically receive a long or  indefinite stream of monetized new  content over time to encourage players  to continue paying to support the game  so nothing specifically about  multiplayer there but the focus is  instead on an  indefinite stream of monetized new  content  i would personally even make the  argument that the new content doesn't  always have to be monetized  you can look at something like animal  crossing new horizons which has provided  free updates for the entire first year  of the game's release and it remains to  be seen what's going to happen after  that first year  they might start doing paid dlc they  could continue to do free updates we  just don't know yet  now overall that definition may sound  fine but we as gamers have been burned  too many times by title sporting this  model  take this reddit post for example which  defines live service games as being the  quote promise of a barely functional  game being sold as a  aaa masterpiece that aims to nickel and  dime users for several years  so there are absolutely concerns when it  comes to this model  i posted a poll here on youtube for you  guys asking can hogwarts legacy work  as a live service game 30 percent of you  said yes there's potential  54 said maybe but i prefer not and only  16  outright said no now i know most of us  are looking forward to the story of  hogwarts legacy and exploring the world  perhaps more than just about anything  else in the game  which means there are fears that parts  of the game could be intentionally held  back  for future dlc or we may see micro  transactions for highly sought after  items the biggest fear by far as i've  seen so many times in the comments on  the videos here is that the game  releases  in a poor or even outright broken state  i'm not going to compare to that game  i'm not going to compare to that game  releasing games as live service can  sometimes trap developers into a  never-ending cycle of trying to fix  a broken game to catch up with the fan  expectations or even giving publishers  the green light to release a broken game  because in the back of their minds and  oh hey this is going to sell well on  name recognition alone  we can just follow it up with the  promise of better things in the future  one of my most played titles ever is the  original destiny which released in a  state that many found frustrating and  even  unacceptable i'm looking at you purple  engrams decrypting into blues  to bungie's credit they would eventually  turn destiny into an incredibly fun  title with a passionate  passionate fan base and yet now they  find themselves on shaky ground once  again  with destiny 2. so we know their  concerns but how does hogwarts legacy  avoid those and deliver an incredible  game that can still  work as live service and keep the fans  not only  tolerant of it but happy and excited  about the live service options  for one they should focus on fulfilling  their initial promise to fans and that  was to make a  story driven action rpg set in the  wizarding world  this has got to be at the forefront guys  this needs to be number one if anyone  from avalanche hears this  you guys have to keep that at the top of  the priority list  now when it comes to the live service  component guys the reason that i am  excited and actually a little bit  optimistic  about this is that this means hogwarts  legacy could potentially be a game  that lives on for months and even years  if it's properly supported  alright so stick with me guys imagine a  post-launch dlc that saw our character  journey  to other wizarding schools or doing a  summer internship at the ministry  of magic seriously like that one has me  so excited could you imagine if you  finish up your first year or whatever  fifth year whenever we're starting at  hogwarts and then maybe you meet a  contact along the story journey where  they work at the ministry you want to  train to be an r and you get to go on  all sorts of these adventures  from the ministry of magic as your kind  of hub yes  sign me up i will pay for that dlc make  it happen  avalanche personally i'm expecting the  main hogwarts legacy game to take place  over the span of one school year but how  great would it be if we got to go on new  adventures and quest with them  throughout  the summer maybe we travel the world  with one of our favorite professors over  the summer to study magical creatures  from other countries or go hunting for  obscure magical artifacts  maybe all of the above one other area of  the wizarding world that seems like it's  just  made for live service would have to be  quidditch  it's something so many fans have asked  for and i think it would work  very well with a live service model  imagine all the different broom  customization options and different  equipment you could have on your player  there could be time trials seasons and  all sorts of different challenges built  around quidditch  personally i like the idea of the added  content sticking with our character from  the main game but  if they wanted to branch out even  further they could always do a dlc  around the triwizard tournament it's an  event in wizarding world history that is  perfect for a video game  unfortunately the timeline just doesn't  match up with the late 1800s of the  hogwarts legacy story  look i'm gonna be honest with you guys i  could go on and on with ideas for how  hogwarts legacy could absolutely  nail the live service experience but now  i'm gonna turn it over  to you guys let me know in the comments  what you'd like to see and if you're new  here be sure and check out our full  hogwarts legacy playlist on the right  side of your screen  as always thank you guys so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon

